    "title": "How Is Ice Made Crystal Clear? 🧊 #shorts",
    "description": "Normal ice is cloudy. This one is crystal clear. 🧊\n\nIn a normal freezer, water freezes from every side at once and traps air and minerals in the middle, which is the cloudy part. Clear-ice makers like New York's Hundredweight Ice use machines that freeze big blocks from the bottom up while a pump keeps the water moving, so bubbles escape. The blocks are then sawed into cubes, about 15,000 a day. What started with a bartender became a $2.5 million business in 2024, according to Business Insider.\n\nThe priciest thing in your drink might be the ice. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
